SCIENTIFIC SCOPE
- Scenario thresholds are inherited from Script 07; no new thresholds are optimized here.
- Terciles and P25/P75 are evaluated as principal quantile-based candidates.
- The data-driven partition is retained as a sensitivity analysis.
- Kruskal-Wallis evaluates global distributional differences.
- Pairwise Mann-Whitney tests use Holm multiplicity correction.
- Jonckheere-Terpstra evaluates the prespecified Low -> Medium -> High ordering.
- Bootstrap intervals quantify sampling uncertainty and do not constitute the later Monte Carlo simulation.
- No observations are deleted.
- No probability distribution is selected.
- No Monte Carlo stochastic model is performed.
- No discrete-event simulation is performed.
- No causal interpretation is imposed.

